sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch05-18> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Among 2D template constraints that also require one template to appear somewhere, systematic search over more than 18 million constraints finds that the first constraint forcing a non-repetitive pattern (number 18762389) forces a unique nested pattern.";
    dc:type "mathematical";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The simplest constraint forcing a non-repetitive pattern forces a nested one";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 5, “Two Dimensions and Beyond”; section “Systems Based on Constraints” (from p. 210), p. 218. Scope: two-dimensional template constraints with a required-template condition"
}
